### Fingerprints (only if no path)

- **djao-trading**: MM / V2 ladder, Bybit, OHLCV, Grafana/Mimir, PAVN trading shards, `@djao-trading/*`, Discord trading (`!status`, `!trade`)
- **xaolonist.eth**: blog post, cover, styleguide, Suno, forge / the-way / pentacles / all-blue, `@aethery`, anh4gs.xyz
- **date-society**: dating society, invite / match / KYC, datesociety.xyz, `@date-society/*`, Meet fewer

`_docs/` and `shared/` exist in **djao-trading** and **date-society** — never route on those alone. Use the filename, `@djao-trading/shared` vs `@date-society/shared`, or topic. Astro = xaolonist blog **or** date-society `web/`. NestJS / Discord = djao `trading-bot` **or** date-society `api`.

## After picking a repo

- All reads / writes / shell / git use that root (`working_directory` or absolute paths).
- Follow **that** repo's `AGENTS.md` / `CLAUDE.md` / skills.
- Ignore other repos' always-applied procedures when they conflict (GitNexus, MM north-star, `trading-bot` jest paths apply **only** to djao-trading).
- If the target was not named explicitly, say the chosen repo in one short clause before working.

## Examples

- `sửa trading-bot/src/trading/position-reload.ts` → **djao-trading**
- `xem _docs/26-08-13-order-flow-monitor-metrics-plan.md` → **djao-trading** (unique filename)
- `viết post the-way, cover.jpg trong src/content/blog/` → **xaolonist.eth**
- `update api Discord module` + no trading-bot files → **date-society**; if also MM / `!trade` → ask
